WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.040
Pandemic nightmares. Twitter scandals. And&nbsp;
the master plan to end all master plans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.120
Where’s Phase 4 of the MCU headed?&nbsp;
Depends on which universe you're in.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.120
Kevin Feige has never made it a secret that&nbsp;
he likes to plan out projects in the MCU far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.520
in advance. Back in August 2013, he revealed&nbsp;
that he had already been discussing films in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.600
the franchise that would release as late as&nbsp;
2021. The following year, he announced that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.800
Marvel had plans for motion pictures laid out&nbsp;
through 2028. In a 2016 interview with Collider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.880
Feige confirmed that Marvel Studios had specific&nbsp;
movies in mind that it wanted to release on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.760
handful of 2020 release dates; even then, he&nbsp;
seemed to know just how Phase Four would pan out.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.160
Feige has also been open about the fact that,&nbsp;
sometimes, these plans do change — such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.080
the studio's team-up with Sony to produce the&nbsp;
Spider-Man movies. But there are still always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.195
ambitions in place for what the future of&nbsp;
the Marvel Cinematic Universe will look like.

00:00:48.195 --> 00:00:52.960
Rome wasn't built in a day, and the Marvel&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe was not formed overnight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.760
Speaking to Rotten Tomatoes in June 2021, just&nbsp;
as Black Widow was about to premiere in theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.760
Kevin Feige said that the prep work for Phase&nbsp;
Four had largely been done over a five- or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.360
six-year period. However, he also pointed&nbsp;
out that other characters in this stretch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.520
the MCU had been gestating for much longer&nbsp;
than that. Specifically, he noted that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.560
character of Shang-Chi had been worked on in&nbsp;
some way shape, or form for "10 or 15 years."

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.440
That's not just PR hype from Feige, either.&nbsp;
Back in 2005, the Los Angeles Times reported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.440
on the creation of Marvel Studios and its&nbsp;
intent to produce self-financed movies;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.880
it also revealed that one of the characters&nbsp;
eyeballed for a solo movie was Shang-Chi.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.640
"Welcome to the circus."

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.520
Of course, this finally came to&nbsp;
pass in 2021 with Shang-Chi and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.040
the Legend of the Ten Rings. The lengthy&nbsp;
amount of time it took for Shang-Chi to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.480
reach movie theaters isn't the norm for&nbsp;
all Marvel Cinematic Universe projects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.371
but it does reflect how long it took&nbsp;
certain Phase Four projects to come about.

00:01:46.462 --> 00:01:51.040
In April 2017, Kevin Feige explained that&nbsp;
plans were already well underway for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.120
follow-up to the MCU's third phase. Though&nbsp;
he was vague on the specifics at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.360
he did note that there were notions that&nbsp;
the term Phase may be abandoned altogether.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.160
A staple of the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
Universe since its inception,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.320
Feige explained to Collider that what&nbsp;
followed Phase Three would be a "new thing."

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.720
Part of that meant finding a new term to refer to&nbsp;
a collection of Marvel Cinematic Universe titles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.120
or even abandoning the practice of grouping&nbsp;
together various installments in the franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.560
In retrospect, it's easy to see why&nbsp;
Feige would harbor such feelings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.760
given how Avengers: Endgame, the&nbsp;
penultimate entry in Phase Three,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.320
was such a gargantuan game-changer for the Marvel&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe. It would only make sense that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.480
he might want to utilize new terminology for&nbsp;
how the various features are organized. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.320
this potential move never came to pass,&nbsp;
with Kevin Feige officially disclosing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.475
details about Phase Four at the San Diego&nbsp;
International Comic-Con in July 2019.

00:02:39.598 --> 00:02:42.880
After the many delays brought&nbsp;
on by the COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.600
Phase Four of the Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;
began with Black Widow in July 2021. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.520
in an alternate timeline, Phase Four would&nbsp;
have kicked off with a very different feature.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.880
"Welcome to the frickin' Guardians of the Galaxy."

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.840
Initially, the first post-Phase Three&nbsp;
entry in this saga would have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.320
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, which was&nbsp;
penciled in for a May 2020 opening. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.520
three-year gap between Vol. 3 and its&nbsp;
predecessor would have nicely mirrored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.320
the length of time between the first&nbsp;
two Guardians of the Galaxy movies.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.840
Having Phase Four kick off with a buzzy&nbsp;
sequel like Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.680
Vol. 3 would also have proved hugely&nbsp;
beneficial to the franchise. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.840
those plans were scuttled in July 2018 when&nbsp;
James Gunn was fired from the movie after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.080
controversy erupted over the filmmaker's&nbsp;
past controversial tweets. With Gunn gone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.560
there were initially reports that Marvel Studios&nbsp;
still planned to move forward with Vol. 3 and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.600
it out in time for a May 2020 debut. However, Gunn&nbsp;
would eventually be welcomed back to the project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.440
though his commitments to The Suicide Squad&nbsp;
ensured Vol. 3 would have to wait until May&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.718
2023. This opened the door for Black Widow&nbsp;
to take over as the debut Phase Four film.

00:03:42.718 --> 00:03:47.520
As Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 hit movie&nbsp;
theaters, writer/director James Gunn confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.520
his intent to make a third installment in this&nbsp;
sci-fi series. While Gunn reaffirmed even back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.000
in 2017 that this would be the final Guardians&nbsp;
film he would write and direct, he did note that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.760
his influence might be felt in the Marvel&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe beyond that franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.280
Speaking on Facebook Live, Gunn revealed that&nbsp;
he would be helping to mold the vision for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.240
the cosmic side of the Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;
for years to come. Referring to Vol. 3, he said:

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.880
"It will help set up the next ten&nbsp;
to twenty years of Marvel movies."

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.240
Gunn did not specify what kind of Phase&nbsp;
Four projects he could be involved in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:20.240
though this potential influence got sidetracked&nbsp;
once he was temporarily fired from Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.880
of the Galaxy Vol. 3. Gunn's focus on the&nbsp;
DCEU kept him busy in the years before he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.800
started shooting the third Guardians chapter.&nbsp;
Though Gunn has yet to follow up on whether or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.480
not he was able to exert his influence&nbsp;
on the cosmic adventures of Phase Four,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:38.320
it doesn't seem particularly likely — especially&nbsp;
considering his busy schedule outside of the MCU.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.920
Years before Kevin Feige and the Marvel&nbsp;
Studios brass officially confirmed what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.800
projects would make up Phase Four&nbsp;
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.520
the rumor mill attempted to fill in the gaps.&nbsp;
But it wasn't until 2018 that a new concept of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.000
Marvel Cinematic Universe storytelling emerged.&nbsp;
This was when Variety broke the news that Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.800
Studios was developing a collection of TV shows&nbsp;
for the then-upcoming Disney+ streaming platform.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.400
The outlet revealed that these small-screen&nbsp;
endeavors would focus on characters such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.720
as Loki and Wanda Maximoff who hadn't yet&nbsp;
received their own solo big-screen outings.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.400
This news was important for a variety of&nbsp;
reasons, but especially because it revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.800
that Marvel Studios was, for the first time,&nbsp;
planning on moving into the world of television.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.720
Up to this point, small-screen programming&nbsp;
that utilized characters from MCU movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.640
had been made by the studio's sister division,&nbsp;
Marvel Television. But with this new wrinkle in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:27.120
Phase Four, Marvel Studios would be expanding&nbsp;
its narrative horizons. In the process, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:32.351
early rumor guaranteed that Phase Four was going&nbsp;
to be unlike any other Phase in the MCU to date.

00:05:32.351 --> 00:05:36.640
Phase Four's exploration of the world of&nbsp;
television goes far beyond the miniseries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.960
however, as the MCU is also delivering&nbsp;
certain stories as holiday TV specials.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.800
Once the domain of Rankin-Bass programming&nbsp;
like Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.680
Marvel Studios is hoping to tell&nbsp;
grander tales that can also double&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.640
as festive entertainment tied to&nbsp;
the biggest holidays of the year.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.720
The first of these projects was announced in&nbsp;
December 2020: the Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.120
Holiday Special. A longtime passion project for&nbsp;
James Gunn, the production was confirmed by Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:03.520
to act as a kind of prologue to Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy Vol. 3. With this reveal, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.760
became clear that these holiday specials weren't&nbsp;
disposable goofs but essential parts of the Phase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.600
Four narrative. This isn't the only holiday&nbsp;
special on the docket for Phase Four either,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.760
as an untitled Halloween special directed&nbsp;
by Michael Giacchino is also on the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:20.240
rumored to be based on the character Werewolf by&nbsp;
Night. With these two projects, Phase Four has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.506
continued to reshape the way in which the MCU can&nbsp;
tell stories — on both the big and small screen.

00:06:25.506 --> 00:06:29.840
When Kevin Feige first publicly spoke about&nbsp;
the prospect of Marvel Studios making original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.520
programming for the Disney+ platform, he&nbsp;
was very insistent that these shows would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:38.240
not be removed from the continuity of this&nbsp;
franchise's movies. Back in February 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.520
Feige told Comicbook.com that these Disney+&nbsp;
programs would be, quote, "entirely interwoven"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:48.320
with the theatrical slate of Phase Four MCU&nbsp;
releases. This was in sharp contrast to how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:52.560
previous TV shows based on Marvel characters&nbsp;
had tended to function. By and large, they had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.240
been mostly separate from the feature-length&nbsp;
narratives in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.440
And Phase Four of the franchise has&nbsp;
managed to live up to Feige's words.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.360
WandaVision set the stage for Wanda&nbsp;
Maximoff's villainous behavior in Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.120
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,&nbsp;
while Ms. Marvel sets up its titular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:11.200
superhero so that she can serve as one of&nbsp;
the leads of the 2023 project The Marvels.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.680
"Oh, no…"

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:17.280
Black Widow's Yelena Belova showed up&nbsp;
in a guest star capacity on Hawkeye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.440
and it's fair to assume that The Falcon and the&nbsp;
Winter Soldier planted seeds that will one day be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.560
sowed in Thunderbolts. Perhaps most importantly,&nbsp;
Jonathan Majors debuted as a version of Kang the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:31.040
Conqueror on Loki before stepping into a much&nbsp;
larger role in movies such as Ant-Man and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:35.520
Wasp: Quantumania and Avengers: The Kang&nbsp;
Dynasty. It's clear that Feige's mission to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:40.000
narrow the gap between big and small-screen&nbsp;
storytelling has very much come to pass.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.240
Looking back on the Phase Four movies&nbsp;
announced at the San Diego International&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:48.400
Comic-Con panel in 2019, you can&nbsp;
immediately spot a few recognizable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:52.400
titles. Projects such as Doctor Strange&nbsp;
in the Multiverse of Madness and Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:56.320
Love and Thunder were among the most exciting to&nbsp;
be announced at the event — but one Phase Four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.720
film notable for its absence was Spider-Man:&nbsp;
No Way Home. This was despite Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:06.320
Far From Home opening a few weeks before the panel&nbsp;
and going on to crack $1.1 billion worldwide.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:10.160
It would later turn out that its absence&nbsp;
was no mistake, as Sony and Marvel were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:13.440
in the middle of negotiations at the&nbsp;
time over the future of Spider-Man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.680
This would eventually result in the two&nbsp;
companies parting ways in August 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.000
with Sony planning to continue the exploits of&nbsp;
Tom Holland's Spider-Man in their own movies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.960
Eventually, an agreement was signed&nbsp;
that reunited the two companies to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:28.946
produce another solo Spider-Man movie,&nbsp;
resulting in Spider-Man: No Way Home.

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:33.440
In the first three Phases of the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
Universe, it was difficult to figure out how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:37.920
franchise connected to the broader franchise of&nbsp;
Netflix characters such as Daredevil, Jessica&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:43.120
Jones, Luke Cage, and Iron Fist. While these shows&nbsp;
would often reference MCU events or characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:48.640
the movies never returned the gesture. Once&nbsp;
the Marvel/Netflix shows were axed in late 2018&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:53.120
and early 2019, it seemed like this chapter&nbsp;
of Marvel storytelling had come to a close.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:56.800
But then came the absorption of Marvel&nbsp;
Television into Marvel Studios. The two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:01.360
entities had previously been wholly separate,&nbsp;
complicating any potential crossovers between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:05.600
their projects. However, now that they were under&nbsp;
the same umbrella, small-screen Marvel projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:10.560
could be more easily ingrained into the wider MCU.&nbsp;
An especially exciting example of this took place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:15.200
in Spider-Man: No Way Home, in which Charlie&nbsp;
Cox's Matt Murdock makes a cameo appearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:19.280
It was the first time a Netflix character had&nbsp;
appeared in an MCU movie, but it wouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:25.680
the last. Vincent D'Onofrio appeared as Kingpin in&nbsp;
Hawkeye, Cox returned for She-Hulk, and, in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:31.091
Marvel announced Daredevil: Born Again, a&nbsp;
Disney+ series slated for release in 2024.

00:09:31.091 --> 00:09:33.920
To bring to life some of its Disney+ programming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.280
the various branches of the Walt Disney&nbsp;
Company have turned to turning screenplays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:41.440
for unproduced movies into longer limited&nbsp;
series. The most high-profile example of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.000
this so far has been Obi-Wan Kenobi, which&nbsp;
utilized enough key plot points and characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.160
from a planned movie to give that feature's&nbsp;
screenwriter a full credit on the project.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.200
"Hello there."

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:55.920
A lesser known example of this trend can also be&nbsp;
found in one of the Phase Four TV shows, Hawkeye.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.600
Apparently, Hawkeye was still a movie back&nbsp;
when Jeremy Renner first signed on — but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:04.080
would later morph into one of the first Disney+&nbsp;
shows created by Marvel Studios. The studio's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.480
ability to transform a prospective movie into&nbsp;
a TV show with such ease demonstrates that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:12.400
with its small-screen projects, Marvel has&nbsp;
mostly been looking to make elongated movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:16.720
rather than traditional episodic TV shows.&nbsp;
It also reflects the ambitions of Disney as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:20.546
a streaming empire, one that won't let&nbsp;
any feature film script go to waste.

00:10:20.546 --> 00:10:25.440
It's difficult to imagine that only one aspect&nbsp;
of Phase Four's narrative was affected by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:30.320
COVID-19 pandemic. After all, there are so many&nbsp;
movies and TV shows to juggle in this saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:34.560
and so many characters and intertwining storylines&nbsp;
in all of those individual productions, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:39.920
surely a lot must have been changed, right? Well,&nbsp;
apparently not. Speaking to On the Red Carpet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:44.080
Feige claimed that only one significant change&nbsp;
had occurred in response to the pandemic.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:48.640
Per Feige, the shadowy benefactor Contessa&nbsp;
Valentina Allegra de Fontaine was supposed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:53.600
make her MCU debut in Black Widow, in which she&nbsp;
appears in the post-credits scene. Instead, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.520
turned up in The Falcon and the Winter Soldier,&nbsp;
due to the shifting timeline that occurred as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.560
result of COVID-19. While it's doubtful this was&nbsp;
the only change to Phase Four's story informed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:07.171
by the pandemic, it is the only alteration that&nbsp;
Feige has so far been willing to speak about.

00:11:07.336 --> 00:11:12.640
Throughout the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic, movie&nbsp;
studios used streaming services to debut movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:16.640
that never before would have been considered&nbsp;
for small-screen premieres. Would new Pixar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:20.960
titles ever have been thought of as fodder for&nbsp;
straight-to-streaming debuts? Similarly, would a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:26.160
mammoth blockbuster like Dune ever have been given&nbsp;
a simultaneous HBO Max launch in any other era?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:30.880
The global health crisis inspired unprecedented&nbsp;
actions from almost every industry on the planet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:34.320
so it should be no surprise that the&nbsp;
entertainment industry followed suit.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.360
"Well, in 120 years of&nbsp;
movies being in our cinemas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:39.440
we've never had to shut down like this before."

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:43.680
Talking to Rotten Tomatoes, Kevin Feige explained&nbsp;
that, even knowing how the pandemic had affected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:47.280
movie theaters, the feature-length efforts&nbsp;
from Marvel Studios were never considered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.040
for streaming. In this same interview, Feige&nbsp;
recalled how his favorite experiences with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:55.520
these movies involved watching them on the big&nbsp;
screen, surrounded by enthusiastic audiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:59.760
Considering that, Feige noted that he had remained&nbsp;
dedicated to keeping the movies in Phase Four as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:06.186
theatrical events. Only one film, Black Widow, had&nbsp;
a dual release, both in theaters and on Disney+.

00:12:06.398 --> 00:12:11.120
While the MCU has a reputation for maintaining&nbsp;
a long-standing and reliable plan for its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:15.520
productions, the franchise has often been forced&nbsp;
to delay projects under certain circumstances.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:19.360
The Avengers was originally set to&nbsp;
debut in July 2011, for instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:24.720
before being delayed to May 2012. Similarly,&nbsp;
Doctor Strange was postponed by four months from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:30.160
its initial July 2016 bow to ensure that Benedict&nbsp;
Cumberbatch could play the titular superhero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.160
However, Phase Four of the MCU took the&nbsp;
cake in terms of release date shuffles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.520
largely thanks to the ongoing&nbsp;
effects of the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:41.600
Some films in Phase Four moved around more&nbsp;
often than others due to the pandemic. Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.880
Love and Thunder was especially&nbsp;
vulnerable to release date tweaks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:49.920
Initially set for a November 2021 premiere&nbsp;
when it was first announced in July 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:54.080
Love and Thunder would eventually be delayed&nbsp;
multiple times, including briefly scoring a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:59.360
Valentine's Day weekend opening, before settling&nbsp;
on a July 2022 launch date. Other projects such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:04.340
as Black Widow and Eternals also received a year&nbsp;
or more's worth of delays due to the pandemic.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:09.440
For obvious reasons, 2021 was something of&nbsp;
an odd year for the theatrical box office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:14.000
Features came roaring back to movie theaters,&nbsp;
and many managed to do solid box office numbers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:17.920
However, with COVID-19 vaccines still making&nbsp;
their way across the general populace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:22.400
people felt varying degrees of comfort with going&nbsp;
to the movies. This, and plenty of other factors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.080
doubtlessly impacted the worldwide box office&nbsp;
returns of the first three installments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.920
in Phase Four. This trio of projects&nbsp;
scored the lowest worldwide box office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:33.680
hauls for any Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;
project outside of The Incredible Hulk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.960
with Black Widow being only the second project in&nbsp;
this series to make under $400 million globally.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:43.440
However, there is some context needed to&nbsp;
better understand these grosses. For starters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:47.120
Black Widow was given a simultaneous&nbsp;
premium-video-on-demand debut on Disney+,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.920
which doubtlessly cut into its grosses. Even&nbsp;
more importantly, none of these movies were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:57.840
released in China. Every Marvel Studios project&nbsp;
released in this territory from 2017 to 2019&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:03.440
exceeded $100 million, with all three of the&nbsp;
company's 2019 productions grossing over $150&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:08.160
million in China alone. A standard theatrical&nbsp;
box office haul in China would have boosted all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:13.280
three movies past the $500 million worldwide&nbsp;
mark. Still, all three found some form of box&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:17.920
office success — and particularly Shang-Chi,&nbsp;
which was briefly the biggest domestic movie of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:23.200
2021… before Spider-Man: No Way Home returned&nbsp;
the franchise to its former box office glory.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:28.240
"I love you guys." "Thank you."

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:33.120
For Phase 4 of the MCU, Marvel Studios has tried&nbsp;
to forge even deeper bonds than usual with some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:37.520
of its most important talent. This is in sharp&nbsp;
contrast to the previous eras in the company's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:42.240
history. Save for a three-year contract in 2012&nbsp;
keeping Joss Whedon around to work on assorted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:47.120
projects, Marvel Studios hasn't kept filmmakers&nbsp;
under long-term contractual obligations. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:52.000
has made it extra easier for directors like Scott&nbsp;
Derrickson and Jon Watts to leave prospective gigs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:56.000
without having to navigate how it might impact&nbsp;
their contractual obligations to the studio.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.920
But that has changed with Phase Four, with&nbsp;
Ryan Coogler being the most notable example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:04.400
of a director who opted to sign on for the long&nbsp;
haul. As part of his overall contract with Disney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:09.840
Coogler was on the hook to oversee a new Disney+&nbsp;
Marvel show set in Wakanda. At the end of 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:13.920
it was announced that Shang-Chi director Destin&nbsp;
Daniel Cretton would be helming a sequel to that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:18.560
movie, and it soon became clear that he had also&nbsp;
signed a long-term contract with Marvel Studios.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:22.560
Sure enough, in 2022, it was reported&nbsp;
that he would be directing Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:27.360
The Kang Dynasty and overseeing a Wonder Man&nbsp;
series for Disney+. For Phase Four and beyond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:31.703
it seems that Marvel Studios wants to keep&nbsp;
a tight hold of its most talented artists.

